# AI Behavior Rules

## 1. Response style
- Be concise and to the point
- Avoid unnecessary explanation unless asked
- Prefer step-by-step when debugging

## 2. When unclear
- Ask clarifying questions instead of guessing
- Do not assume business logic

## 3. Code output
- Provide clean, production-ready code
- Avoid overengineering
- Prefer readability over complexity

## 4. Debugging
- Always explain root cause first
- Then propose fix
- Then show code if needed

## 5. Consistency
- Do not contradict existing project patterns
- Follow existing folder structure and naming